Fonts embedded in the SHIPPED BINARY
------------------------------------

About polylinker.exe, not about this repository -- which is why the record was
missing until the 2026-07-30 typography pass went looking for it. `bins/pl-gui`
enables eframe's `default_fonts` feature, which pulls `epaint_default_fonts`
0.35.0; that crate `include_bytes!`es four font files, so every distributed copy
of the GUI carries 1,414,020 bytes of third-party font data (16.8% of an 8.4 MB
exe) and its attribution obligations. None of it is checked in here.

Sizes and versions below were read out of the shipped .ttf files' own `name`
tables, not from a changelog. Licence texts travel with the crate, under
`epaint_default_fonts-0.35.0/fonts/`.

  Hack                     309,408 bytes   Version 3.003
    THREE licences at once, and the third is not boilerplate:
      - the Hack work itself: MIT, (c) 2018 Source Foundry Authors
      - the DejaVu work it derives from: committed to the public domain
      - Bitstream Vera Sans Mono: (c) 2003 Bitstream, Inc., BITSTREAM VERA
        LICENSE, with Reserved Font Names "Bitstream" and "Vera". It requires
        the copyright AND TRADEMARK notices to be included in all copies of the
        Font Software typefaces, forbids selling a Font Software typeface by
        itself, and becomes null and void for modified fonts distributed under
        the Vera names. Polylinker embeds it unmodified and sells nothing, so
        what is owed is the notice -- this one.
    Text: fonts/Hack-Regular.txt   https://github.com/source-foundry/Hack

  Ubuntu Light             361,676 bytes   Version 0.83
    UBUNTU FONT LICENCE 1.0. Neither OFL nor Apache-2.0, and so NOT on this
    project's own allow-list for embedded fonts -- recorded as a question for
    Lior rather than presented as settled. UFL does permit bundling and
    embedding; it requires that the fonts and any derivative not be released
    under any other licence.
    Text: fonts/UFL.txt

  Noto Emoji               418,804 bytes   Version 1.05 uh
    SIL Open Font License 1.1.   Text: fonts/OFL.txt
    Load-bearing rather than decorative: U+26A0, the hidden-cut-sites warning
    marker, is absent from BOTH Hack and Ubuntu Light and is served only from
    here or from emoji-icon-font. Turning `default_fonts` off would draw the
    app's safety marker as a tofu box.

  emoji-icon-font          324,132 bytes   Version 1.1
    MIT.   Text: fonts/emoji-icon-font-mit-license.txt

`pl licences` prints the compiled-in feature-database attribution. It does not
yet print this font block, and it should, so the obligation travels with the
binary and not only with the repository.

